WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.359 --> 00:00:07.608
- That day, when the bus
driver asked me to get up,

00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:09.895
I had this feeling come over me,

00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:13.978
it felt like Harriet
Tubman was holding me down,

00:00:13.978 --> 00:00:16.713
hands were holding me down on one shoulder

00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:19.256
and Sojourner Truth hands
were holding me down

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:20.664
on another shoulder,

00:00:20.664 --> 00:00:24.922
and I was glued to the
seat and I could hear

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:28.122
the white passengers
saying, "She gotta move,

00:00:28.122 --> 00:00:29.210
she gotta move.”

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.870
"That's the law, she gotta move."

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.712
and I felt like,

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:36.379
this is my time to take
a stand for justice.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.047
(laughs)

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:47.319
My name is Claudette Colvin,

00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:50.652
and in 1955 I refused to give up my seat

00:00:51.604 --> 00:00:55.771
to a white passenger on the
bus in Montgomery, Alabama,

00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.483
nine months before Rosa Parks.

00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:05.065
I was 15 years old, and the
rule and the segregation

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:08.504
that a white person had
to sit in front of you

00:01:08.504 --> 00:01:10.296
and you sit behind them,

00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:14.409
and so the bus driver asked me to get up.

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:17.317
I was shouting, it's my
constitutional rights,

00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:18.629
I'm not gonna move,

00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:22.796
and that's when the policeman
dragged me off the bus.

00:01:23.911 --> 00:01:27.465
Most people ask me, weren't you afraid?

00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:30.166
Well, I was a teenager, I was afraid,

00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:34.083
but I was more angry at
these white passengers.

00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:37.974
And then, they took me and booked me.

00:01:37.974 --> 00:01:41.558
I still vividly can hear
the sound of the keys go,

00:01:41.558 --> 00:01:44.809
(makes turning sounds)

00:01:44.809 --> 00:01:48.295
and I was terrified
and I starting reciting

00:01:48.295 --> 00:01:49.800
the Lord's Prayer.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.718
"Thou will be done on
Earth as it is in Heaven."

00:01:53.718 --> 00:01:55.446
And I was just praying for help,

00:01:55.446 --> 00:01:59.384
you know, praying that they were
going to let my parents know

00:01:59.384 --> 00:02:00.967
that I was in jail.

00:02:02.008 --> 00:02:04.547
My mom would say, "Claudette,
I think you was anointed

00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:05.992
by God to do this."

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.593
I said, “I don't think so mother,

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:11.760
I just had, I just thought
that this was my right.”

00:02:13.724 --> 00:02:18.042
I just wanted people to
come together and unify

00:02:18.042 --> 00:02:19.757
and fight the segregation.

00:02:19.757 --> 00:02:22.340
(upbeat music)

